    "reason": "The assertion 'self attention --[computes]--> weight matrix' is technically imprecise because self-attention computes a full set of attention scores (weights) which are then applied to value vectors to produce the output representation, not just a single 'weight matrix' as a final result. The relation conflates the intermediate score calculation with the final output generation. Additionally, the term 'weight matrix' is ambiguous; in this context, it refers to the dynamic attention weights derived from Q-K similarity, distinct from the static parameter weight matrices of the network layers. To preserve causal strength and precision, the target should be refined to 'attention scores' or the relation should specify the computation of these scores before aggregation.",
